BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 758.9000000000001 Td (- Work: W=Fs cos\(theta\); if force is perpendicular, W=0.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 747.0000000000001 Td (- Kinetic energy K=\(1/2\)mv^2; gravitational potential near Earth U=mgh; spring energy U_s=\(1/2\)kx^2.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 735.1000000000001 Td (- Work-energy theorem: W_net=Delta K=\(1/2\)m\(v^2-u^2\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 723.2000000000002 Td (- Power P=W/t; energy transferred E=Pt.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 711.3000000000002 Td (- Momentum conservation in a perfectly inelastic collision: m1u1+m2u2=\(m1+m2\)v.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 699.4000000000002 Td (- For F=kx from x=0 to x=a: W=integral\(F dx\)=\(1/2\)ka^2.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 687.5000000000002 Td (- For a falling body without losses: mgh=\(1/2\)mv^2, so v=sqrt\(2gh\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 675.6000000000003 Td (- Stopping force magnitude for constant force: |F|=|W|/distance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 48 663.7000000000003 Td (Use each equation only when its assumptions apply; keep units consistent.) Tj ET
